@*
    Areas/POS/Views/Dashboard/HoursWiseSalesDataView.cshtml

    The hour-by-hour breakdown, opened from the "Hours Wise Sales" link on the
    Sales tab. This view was NOT among the files carried over from the Call
    Centre project - the controller renders it by name, so the tab threw until
    it existed. It is rebuilt from what Dashboard.js does with it:

        $('#HoursWiseSalesDataView').html(result.view);
        $('#HourlyChartGroupBy').val(result.GroupByFlag);
        genHourlyWiseSalesBarGraph(result.hourlyWiseSalesData);

    So it has to contain the chart container (id="hourswisesalesbarchart"), the
    group-by dropdown (id="HourlyChartGroupBy") and a way back. The chart is
    drawn by Chartkick after this HTML lands, which is why the div is empty.
*@
<div class="row">
    <div class="col-lg-12 mb-3">
        <div class="card h-100">
            <div class="card-header p-2 border-0 bg-dark">
                <div class="d-flex justify-content-between align-items-center">
                    <label class="text-white">Hours Wise Sales</label>

                    <div class="d-flex align-items-center">
                        @* Values match what sp_DashbordSalesData groups by:
                           1 branch, 2 invoice type, 3 everything together. *@
                        <select id="HourlyChartGroupBy" class="form-control form-control-sm mr-2"
                                style="width:auto;">
                            <option value="1">By Branch</option>
                            <option value="2">By Order Type</option>
                            <option value="3">All Together</option>
                        </select>

                        <input type="button" value="Back" class="btn btn-primary btn-sm"
                               onclick="BackToMainTab();" />
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="card-body p-2">
                @* Chartkick renders into this by id. Height is set here rather
                   than left to the chart: an unsized container collapses to
                   nothing before the first draw and the page jumps. *@
                <div id="hourswisesalesbarchart" style="height:420px;"></div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
